[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said one issue, one fix queued. Its reports said otherwise: they were
merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and a subject
line says that a date is wrong, not why. Read by tenant, form and body, the merged reports are
three problems. Each has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed and the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day
shift is neither. Nothing in #4471 fixes it, so it is still open.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

- **`parser`** (fixed, `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`): the shared parser read every
  date month first. Our tenants all write the day first, so day and month swapped: 7 April came
  out as 4 July. This is what #4471 described.
- **`hint`** (won't fix, form retired): the booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date
  field but read the date day first. People typed what the hint said and the date swapped. Only
  form reports from booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix did not touch the form; retiring it did.
- **`shift`** (open): the booking moves by one day, no swap; the same meeting shows Tuesday in
  Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. A timezone or day-boundary bug. The desk noted these
  (`desk-notes.json`, `oneDayMove`) and filed them under `parser` by tenant, so they went out
  with #4471. The parser fix does not change them.

## How it was counted

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so some reports come twice.
- Cause by tenant locale, booking form and channel (`causes.ts`), not by intake tag, the same view
  as [#4471's table](/kb/incidents/4471). Intake guesses from the browser; the table shows how
  often it guessed a different cause.
- The `shift` reports are the desk's own list, checked against every report body: the others
  quote a day/month swap or no comparable dates.

## For the desk

- A one-day move is not a swap. Send it to the `shift` ticket, not to `parser`.
- Before merging into a ticket, check that the report has the same cause, not the same subject.
  The [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already shows the difference.

